      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure what you mean about a wrapper trait, but what you have here now seems alright.\n\nI wonder about the context save and restore case though, as that\u0027s on a more performance-critical path. I guess most extensions won\u0027t need to save and restore any context, so checking whether each extension is present twice on every context switch seems like an unnecessary cost. We could instead say that `save_context` and `restore_context` are responsible for doing the check. That way for most extensions (with no context) they could continue to be no-ops, and only the few extensions that actually have context would actually have the check.",
